I was reading the notes from last year's Netfilter developers workshop
and I noticed that the group discussed the need for a standard set of
benchmarking tests for packet filtering and a set of tools.  It seems
that there is already a plan in the works to develop a set of tools?  I
was wondering what the status of this is?  I'm also wondering if there
is a concrete plan for developing a specification for a packet filtering
benchmark.  Is there some way to get involved in the process? =20

I haven't been able to find an standard plan, and it seems that many
performance numbers I see are for extremely simple rulesets.  Perhaps I
am just looking in the wrong places, so if anyone can educate me about
what the "standard" benchmark used for packet filtering is, I would
appreciate it.

Thanks!
Kristen
